    {
      "id": "reserved-subgroup-id-mode",
      "description": "subgroup stream header with Type 0x16, whose SUBGROUP_ID_MODE is the reserved 0b11 — must close the session. Section 11.4.2: \"The following Type values are invalid. If an endpoint receives a stream header with any of these Type values, it MUST close the session with a PROTOCOL_VIOLATION: Type values with SUBGROUP_ID_MODE set to 0b11: 0x16, 0x17, 0x1E, 0x1F, 0x36, 0x37, 0x3E, 0x3F, 0x56, 0x57, 0x5E, 0x5F, 0x76, 0x77, 0x7E, 0x7F. This mode is reserved for future use.\" Distinct from a Type outside the defined form, which no table assigns at all; this one is inside the form and separately named invalid. The bytes after the Type are those of the subgroup-single-object vector, which decodes.",
      "hex": "160100800004deadbeef",
      "error": "invalid_type",
      "error_detail": "subgroup stream Type 0x16 sets SUBGROUP_ID_MODE to the reserved 0b11"
    },
    {
      "id": "type-bit-4-clear",
      "description": "subgroup stream header with Type 0x20, whose bit 4 is clear. Section 11.4.2: \"Type values that do not match the form 0b0XX1XXXX (i.e., Type values outside the ranges 0x10..0x1F, 0x30..0x3F, 0x50..0x5F, and 0x70..0x7F, or values where bit 4 is not set).\" Bit 4 is the one bit every SUBGROUP_HEADER Type sets, so a value without it names no stream this draft assigns, and Section 3.4 is the rule that answers it: \"An endpoint that receives an unknown stream type MUST close the session.\" Draft-20 states bit 4 as a condition on a flags field instead and answers the same byte with invalid_type. The bytes after the Type are those of the subgroup-single-object vector, which decodes.",
      "hex": "200100800004deadbeef",
      "error": "unknown_message",
      "error_detail": "stream Type 0x20 has bit 4 clear and is assigned to nothing"
    },
    {
      "id": "type-above-127",
      "description": "subgroup stream header whose Type decodes to 144, encoded as the minimal two-byte varint 8090. Section 11.4.2: \"Type values that do not match the form 0b0XX1XXXX (i.e., Type values outside the ranges 0x10..0x1F, 0x30..0x3F, 0x50..0x5F, and 0x70..0x7F, or values where bit 4 is not set).\" Bit 4 is set and SUBGROUP_ID_MODE is 0b00, so the value clears every condition but the form's leading zero, and bit 7 is what puts it outside. Every Type the form admits is below 0x80 and occupies one byte; the width is refused before the value, because narrowing a two-byte field to its low octet would read this as 0x90 and a 0x8010 as an ordinary subgroup header. The bytes after the Type are those of the subgroup-single-object vector, which decodes.",
      "hex": "80900100800004deadbeef",
      "error": "unknown_message",
      "error_detail": "stream Type 144 is outside the form the draft defines"
    },
